1
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:41,200
Vin.

2
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:53,360
Easy... easy.

3
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,480
Take a sip.

4
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:18,520
How do you feel?

5
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:20,440
Feeling better?

6
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:24,680
I...

7
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:27,640
I...

8
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:31,400
How did I end up here?

9
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:35,639
You had malaria.

10
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:37,559
You were unconscious for days.

11
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:40,039
Good thing they got
you to the doctor in time.

12
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:43,199
As for Sila, he's at the
reeducation camp right now.

13
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:44,479
Just wait-

14
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,839
another week or two until you recover.

15
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:48,600
Then you will have to go there too.

16
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:51,480
A reeducation camp?

17
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:52,960
Mm-hmm.

18
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:59,040
It's set up by the government for people who used
to be in the jungle before returning to the city.

19
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:02,479
But you don't have to worry, Vin.

20
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,680
I'll be your guarantor.

21
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,279
You and Sila will stay there about a month,

22
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:08,120
then you'll be released.

23
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:59,000
"When Light Fades" (Episode 8)

24
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:03,239
(Order 66/2523)

25
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:05,559
(opened the way for those with-)

26
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,479
(differing political
beliefs and ideologies, )

27
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:09,359
(including Communist Party members)

28
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:12,839
(and civilians who fled into the
jungle to escape suppression, )

29
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:15,759
(to lay down their weapons
and leave the jungle)

30
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:18,399
(to become contributors
to Thailand's development.)

31
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:22,239
(They will receive amnesty
for all political charges)

32
00:03:22,264 --> 00:03:24,656
(and be able to participate
in the elections) Aunt La Or.

33
00:03:24,681 --> 00:03:27,321
(In accordance with
democratic principles) Oh, Dan.

34
00:03:28,279 --> 00:03:30,399
I was just about to call you.

35
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:33,640
Is Vin close to being released yet, dear?

36
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:37,920
Well...

37
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:42,560
There's something I need to tell you.

38
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:50,120
Mom.

39
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,040
Vin.

40
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,640
Mom.

41
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,560
Then who brought me out?

42
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:26,920
Sila and Sin.

43
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:31,839
They brought you to the military camp,

44
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:33,480
then went back into the jungle.

45
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:36,719
When they brought you back,
you had to be searched.

46
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:38,400
So I kept this for you.

47
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,160
Sin.

48
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:12,880
I... I, I'm here.

49
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:20,360
I'm always with you, Vin.

50
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,840
Grilled sticky rice with meat?

51
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:16,840
Never seen that before.

52
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:23,040
I was afraid some kid might be hungry,
so I added pork.

53
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:25,720
- Mm.
- How is it?

54
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:31,920
You know...

55
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,840
when I first met you,

56
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:38,880
you were so cold and emotionless.

57
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,240
I'm human too.

58
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:42,840
How could I not have feelings?

59
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:47,080
When my parents died,
I cried for a very long time.

60
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:56,520
Then how did you get through it?

61
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,760
It was really hard.

62
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:03,880
Maybe because of the “Joy Game.”

63
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:07,080
My mother taught me how to play it.

64
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:09,800
It helped a lot.

65
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,120
The Joy Game?

66
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:13,760
What's that?

67
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:15,400
I've never heard of it.

68
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:41,560
Aren't you going to eat too?

69
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:43,000
You keep on eating.

70
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:45,599
Otherwise you'll faint again
and I'll have to carry you.

71
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:46,640
Heavy as you are...

72
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:48,040
open your mouth.

73
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:50,920
But if I'm full, I want
us to be full together.

74
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:52,720
If we starve, we starve together.

75
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:54,920
Come on, let me feed you now.

76
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:58,600
Here, open up.

77
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:06,320
What's this? Don't act all shy now.

78
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:09,160
So what about that Joy Game of yours?

79
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:11,920
Tell me about it. Come on, tell me.

80
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:14,240
Let me hear it.

81
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:18,560
You speak your suffering out loud,

82
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:22,280
then you find the good
hidden inside that suffering.

83
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:26,120
Once you vent it out, you feel lighter.

84
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:28,559
Suffering...

85
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:30,160
has a good side too?

86
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:35,000
Everything has two sides.

87
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:40,160
Like today, for example.

88
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,120
The sun is blazing hot.

89
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:43,560
Mm-hmm.

90
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:46,920
But the good thing is,
the sky becomes clear.

91
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,040
And at night,

92
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:50,920
the stars become beautiful.

93
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:52,720
Mm-hmm.

94
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:54,960
And so we can watch the stars together.

95
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:17,040
I'm sorry that I came
so far away from home.

96
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:20,480
And I don't even know
when I'll ever return again.

97
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:26,280
But there is something good about it.

98
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:29,120
The good thing is...

99
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:31,280
I met someone here

100
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:35,800
that I love very much.

101
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:34,400
Why was this meeting called?

102
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:39,240
The Party has issued orders.

103
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:45,240
After the government announced its policy,

104
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:50,040
many people surrendered
and laid down their weapons.

105
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:53,720
So the Party issued new orders.

106
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:57,240
Anyone who still wants to keep fighting

107
00:11:58,360 --> 00:12:00,040
must all cross over to the other side.

108
00:12:00,680 --> 00:12:02,800
As for us, we destroy the documents

109
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:05,560
and follow later.

110
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:09,480
And appoint Comrade Yue
as the new leader instead.

111
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:40,120
(Ravin ChaiChan 12 Rd.Maha Chai,
Sumranrath, Pranakorn, ฺBangkok)

112
00:14:00,393 --> 00:14:02,433
[A very sad letter to Vin apologizing
without the intention of seeing him again.]

113
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:05,239
Mom, I'm home.

114
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:06,400
Vin.

115
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:17,343
Mom, are you okay? Why
do you look so stressed?

116
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:22,600
Ah... it's nothing, dear. Sit down first.

117
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:27,919
How did the internship interview go?

118
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:29,080
I passed, Mom.

119
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:32,439
Once I told them I wanted
to become a journalist,

120
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:34,160
they kept talking with me for ages.

121
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:37,199
Good. That's wonderful.

122
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,600
My son is the best.

123
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:40,639
Go on, go take a shower.

124
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:42,919
I'll make something
delicious for you to eat.

125
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:43,480
Okay, Mom.
Go.

126
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:12,159
Comrade Roong should've already-

127
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:13,640
sent the last group across safely.

128
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:17,160
We should hurry too.

129
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:35,520
I'm done.

130
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:43,040
It's not locked, Mom.

131
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:46,680
Vin.

132
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:48,400
Dan.

133
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:51,079
I got off work early today, so...

134
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,400
I stopped by for dinner.

135
00:16:53,040 --> 00:16:54,680
Aunt La Or told me to get you.

136
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:15,120
Do you still think about him?

137
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:24,280
And...

138
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:29,440
Do you still love him?

139
00:17:33,720 --> 00:17:35,160
I'm not sure.

140
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:50,000
Do you remember what I told
you that night at Chan Siao Cave?

141
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:59,840
I know you don't think of me that way.

142
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:09,559
But can you give me a chance?

143
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:11,400
We can take things slowly.

144
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:19,120
But...

145
00:18:20,017 --> 00:18:22,736
But with him, you can't even answer-

146
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:24,360
whether you still love him or not.

147
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:28,800
Why can't it be me, Vin?

148
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:34,000
It's not something that
can just be anyone, Dan.

149
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:51,560
Where did I lose to him, Vin?

150
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:57,240
Because you're not him.

151
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:12,480
Even if he's dead,

152
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:15,400
or even if we never meet again,

153
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:20,120
I will always see you as a brother.

154
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:26,920
Just as a brother.

155
00:19:59,040 --> 00:20:00,040
What's wrong, Comrade?

156
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:01,840
Excited about crossing over?

157
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:04,520
What's there to be excited about?

158
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:08,079
Come on, if we make it across,
you'll become the leader.

159
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:09,040
Aren't you happy?
Hey,

160
00:20:10,520 --> 00:20:11,520
let me rest first.

161
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:28,680
Nature calls.

162
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:30,760
Comrade Fah,

163
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:32,919
watch the bags for me, okay?

164
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:34,199
OK.

165
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:35,200
Be right back.

166
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,120
I'm going to refill the water.
Mm.

167
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:12,920
Hey!

168
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:16,720
Ouch!

169
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,239
What the hell are you doing, Nop?!

170
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:20,960
You took everything away from me.

171
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:23,600
So you're trying to kill me now?

172
00:21:23,720 --> 00:21:24,080
Huh?!

173
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:25,999
You're going to kill me?!

174
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Huh?!

175
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:31,280
Hngh!

176
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:36,840
I followed every single rule.

177
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:40,479
I sacrificed everything for the Party.

178
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:42,519
And in the end, after one mistake,

179
00:21:42,520 --> 00:21:43,879
the Party threw me away like trash

180
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:45,439
and put you in my place.

181
00:21:45,440 --> 00:21:46,360
What about me?

182
00:21:46,361 --> 00:21:47,679
I did everything for the Party.

183
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:49,119
For the ideology,

184
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:50,120
huh?!

185
00:21:53,120 --> 00:21:54,879
Stop hiding behind ideology already.

186
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:56,919
I killed people to protect you.

187
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:58,319
I fled into the jungle with you.

188
00:21:58,320 --> 00:22:00,960
I never wanted anything from the Party.

189
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:02,920
I always saw you as my friend.

190
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:04,720
How could you do this to me?

191
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:38,960
Vin.

192
00:22:41,040 --> 00:22:42,040
What are you doing?

193
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:43,560
Planting vegetables, bro.

194
00:22:44,600 --> 00:22:45,600
Planting vegetables?

195
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:48,479
Well, from what I remember,

196
00:22:48,480 --> 00:22:50,200
you hated vegetables when you were little.

197
00:22:51,320 --> 00:22:53,360
Before I knew it, you've already
skipped ahead to growing them yourself.

198
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:55,279
Back when I was living at the base,

199
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:56,559
there wasn't any meat to eat.

200
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:57,680
So I had to eat vegetables.

201
00:22:58,400 --> 00:22:59,879
After eating them for a while,

202
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,240
I ended up liking them.

203
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:04,240
Talking about it now makes
me think of them again.

204
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:06,400
I miss them so much.

205
00:23:17,840 --> 00:23:19,080
Bro...

206
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:24,120
I'm sorry.

207
00:23:26,600 --> 00:23:27,600
Mm.

208
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:32,160
Actually... I've been trying to move on.

209
00:23:32,920 --> 00:23:33,920
But now I understand.

210
00:23:34,760 --> 00:23:35,560
Love doesn't necessarily-

211
00:23:35,561 --> 00:23:37,680
mean staying close or owning someone.

212
00:23:40,280 --> 00:23:41,759
Stepping back a little,

213
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:43,760
while still getting to
stay in each other's lives,

214
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:45,120
might be better.

215
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:50,120
Let's see what you're planting.

216
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:52,640
Vin!

217
00:23:54,920 --> 00:23:55,920
Sila!

218
00:24:01,240 --> 00:24:02,800
- Vin!
- Hey, Mada!

219
00:24:05,280 --> 00:24:07,400
- Damn, I missed you so much.
- Vin.

220
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:09,400
It's been forever.

221
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:11,640
Weren't you supposed to get out next year?

222
00:24:12,080 --> 00:24:13,759
We got our sentence reduced,
so we were released earlier.

223
00:24:13,760 --> 00:24:14,839
Sila came to pick me up.

224
00:24:14,840 --> 00:24:16,719
He especially wanted to surprise you.

225
00:24:16,720 --> 00:24:18,039
- Hey, seriously?
- How have you been?

226
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:19,040
Vin.

227
00:24:19,520 --> 00:24:20,400
Oh, Dan.
Hello.

228
00:24:20,961 --> 00:24:22,080
Hello. Hello.

229
00:24:22,640 --> 00:24:23,936
Go spend time with your friends first.

230
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:25,199
I'm going to see Aunt La Or for a bit.

231
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:26,200
Okay, bro.

232
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:30,679
Man, it's been so long.

233
00:24:30,680 --> 00:24:31,719
I missed you so much.

234
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:33,439
Hey, since we haven't
seen each other in forever,

235
00:24:33,440 --> 00:24:34,440
Today...

236
00:24:34,480 --> 00:24:35,400
should we celebrate a little today?

237
00:24:35,401 --> 00:24:36,999
Same as always. The usual recipe.

238
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:38,439
- Sure.
- I can handle it.

239
00:24:38,440 --> 00:24:39,720
Hey, you have to come with me.

240
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:41,240
Wooo.

241
00:24:42,160 --> 00:24:43,160
No, no, no!

242
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:44,200
Hey, Vin!

243
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:45,800
- Hey!
- Are you messing with me?

244
00:24:46,440 --> 00:24:47,120
Just kidding, just kidding.

245
00:24:47,121 --> 00:24:48,400
Go. Go. Go.

246
00:24:53,560 --> 00:24:55,359
Baan Saeng Dao Base has already fallen.

247
00:24:55,360 --> 00:24:56,479
The ones who still wanted to fight all-

248
00:24:56,480 --> 00:24:57,599
crossed over to the other side.

249
00:24:57,600 --> 00:24:58,600
Including Comrade Yue.

250
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:01,440
Even though the base is gone now,

251
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:02,920
for us,

252
00:25:03,720 --> 00:25:04,880
it was a classroom of life.

253
00:25:05,680 --> 00:25:07,400
It taught us to see people as human beings.

254
00:25:08,120 --> 00:25:09,120
Um...

255
00:25:09,640 --> 00:25:11,599
That place really was a life lesson.

256
00:25:11,600 --> 00:25:13,719
We've seen that no matter what system...

257
00:25:13,720 --> 00:25:14,560
or what beliefs people follow,

258
00:25:14,561 --> 00:25:16,880
every one of them has both pros and cons.

259
00:25:18,560 --> 00:25:19,880
The chaos comes from the people-

260
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:22,320
who misuse them.

261
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:31,800
When he brought you to the military camp.

262
00:25:32,360 --> 00:25:33,360
Vin had malaria.

263
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:37,840
There was no medicine at the base.

264
00:25:42,160 --> 00:25:43,200
We needed a doctor.

265
00:25:44,320 --> 00:25:45,320
I'm begging you.

266
00:25:51,120 --> 00:25:53,080
He kissed you without hesitation.

267
00:25:53,920 --> 00:25:55,240
Even I was shocked when I saw it.

268
00:25:58,400 --> 00:26:00,280
You knew from that moment, didn't you?

269
00:26:02,320 --> 00:26:04,080
That was when everything
became clear to me.

270
00:26:06,520 --> 00:26:08,480
And you don't find me disgusting?

271
00:26:10,280 --> 00:26:12,520
Before entering the jungle,
I couldn't accept it either.

272
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:14,639
But after seeing him fight with everything-

273
00:26:14,640 --> 00:26:16,839
he had just to get you to a doctor,

274
00:26:16,840 --> 00:26:18,719
my whole perspective changed.

275
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:20,759
I realized that being able to love someone,

276
00:26:20,760 --> 00:26:22,799
and having them love you back,

277
00:26:22,800 --> 00:26:25,360
that alone is already enough.

278
00:26:28,640 --> 00:26:29,960
If everyone could think like you,

279
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:31,440
things would be better.

280
00:26:32,480 --> 00:26:34,160
Maybe we won't see it in our generation.

281
00:26:35,040 --> 00:26:36,759
But I believe that...

282
00:26:36,760 --> 00:26:37,760
one day,

283
00:26:37,761 --> 00:26:39,479
someone will dare to think differently-

284
00:26:39,480 --> 00:26:41,519
and do something new to change the country.

285
00:26:41,520 --> 00:26:42,999
But I don't want to wait.

286
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:44,840
We want it to happen in our generation.

287
00:26:47,080 --> 00:26:48,080
Mm.

288
00:26:49,440 --> 00:26:51,559
May I come in to speak with
you for a moment, please?

289
00:26:51,560 --> 00:26:53,199
Of course. Please, come in.

290
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:54,200
Yes.

291
00:26:56,080 --> 00:26:57,080
Please come in.

292
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:03,439
We received a report

293
00:27:03,440 --> 00:27:05,840
about an unidentified male
body found in Nan Province.

294
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:08,760
The victim face was
beaten beyond recognition.

295
00:27:10,040 --> 00:27:11,279
But during investigation,

296
00:27:11,280 --> 00:27:13,520
we found that the firearm
had your name engraved on it.

297
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:21,800
(Ravin ChaiChan)

298
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:27,000
Mm.

299
00:27:29,520 --> 00:27:30,640
Why are you giving me a gun?

300
00:27:30,920 --> 00:27:32,320
You want me to shoot now?

301
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:34,240
Look carefully first.

302
00:27:39,120 --> 00:27:43,040
(Sasin Ngaochan) That way,
you'll feel like I'm always beside you.

303
00:27:44,640 --> 00:27:46,720
I want you by my side all the time too.

304
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:51,160
This part is mine.

305
00:27:55,720 --> 00:28:00,640
(Ravin ChaiChan)

306
00:28:02,760 --> 00:28:04,560
Do you happen to know
who might've done this?

307
00:28:05,040 --> 00:28:06,639
Right now, we still don't know.

308
00:28:06,640 --> 00:28:08,239
And there are no witnesses yet.

309
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:10,039
The body was abandoned deep in the forest.

310
00:28:10,040 --> 00:28:11,359
If possible, I'd like to ask you

311
00:28:11,360 --> 00:28:13,880
to come give a statement
at the police station.

312
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:22,680
I'll go with you.

313
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:39,240
Vin, where are you going, dear?

314
00:28:39,840 --> 00:28:40,840
I'm going to Nan.

315
00:28:40,841 --> 00:28:42,601
I need to make sure
whether it's really him.

316
00:28:44,440 --> 00:28:45,480
Who is that guy?

317
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:48,320
Why are you this desperate
to go to Nan right now?

318
00:28:49,920 --> 00:28:50,920
Vin.

319
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:52,960
Vin.

320
00:28:54,800 --> 00:28:55,800
Vin.

321
00:28:56,480 --> 00:28:59,800
I can't bear to watch
you leaving like that again.

322
00:29:01,720 --> 00:29:02,720
Do you know, Vin?

323
00:29:04,600 --> 00:29:06,480
That day when I woke
up and couldn't find you,

324
00:29:08,440 --> 00:29:11,240
I ran everywhere searching
for you like a madwoman.

325
00:29:13,040 --> 00:29:15,480
When Dan told me you
had gone into the jungle,

326
00:29:17,920 --> 00:29:20,640
even though I felt relieved
that you were still alive,

327
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:26,520
I never slept peacefully again,
not even for a single night.

328
00:29:28,880 --> 00:29:31,240
Are you going to leave your
mother again today, dear?

329
00:29:33,840 --> 00:29:34,960
I'm sorry...

330
00:29:36,320 --> 00:29:37,880
I'm sorry for making you worry.

331
00:29:44,760 --> 00:29:46,320
I know your heart is breaking.

332
00:29:47,360 --> 00:29:49,120
But he's gone no matter what.

333
00:29:50,840 --> 00:29:52,080
Sometimes...

334
00:29:52,840 --> 00:29:54,800
we have to let it go, dear.

335
00:29:57,680 --> 00:29:59,240
Mom.

336
00:30:29,280 --> 00:30:30,440
Cork tree' flower cigarettes

337
00:30:31,720 --> 00:30:32,840
help with allergies.

338
00:30:34,040 --> 00:30:35,040
Mm,

339
00:30:35,120 --> 00:30:36,120
try it.

340
00:30:41,680 --> 00:30:43,000
How is it? Do you like it?

341
00:30:44,080 --> 00:30:45,319
Yeah, I do.

342
00:30:45,320 --> 00:30:46,800
It smells nice. Tastes good too.

343
00:30:48,240 --> 00:30:50,639
Why don't you roll a new one?

344
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:52,319
This one already has my saliva on it.

345
00:30:52,320 --> 00:30:53,400
Get a new one.

346
00:31:02,400 --> 00:31:03,480
Although while we're here,

347
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:06,040
and I couldn't show my feelings too much.

348
00:31:07,360 --> 00:31:08,880
But that doesn't mean I feel nothing.

349
00:31:13,960 --> 00:31:15,120
What do you feel?

350
00:31:20,040 --> 00:31:21,960
I feel that you're someone very special.

351
00:31:24,880 --> 00:31:26,120
And I want to take care of you.

352
00:31:26,440 --> 00:31:28,880
(I just want to wake up)

353
00:31:30,600 --> 00:31:33,160
(without tears…)

354
00:31:34,440 --> 00:31:37,279
Comrade Yue! Comrade Yue!
(Wishing it would all fade away.)

355
00:31:37,280 --> 00:31:38,000
(Wishing it would all fade away.)
Comrade Saeng!

356
00:31:38,880 --> 00:31:39,240
(Begging the wind to carry it off.)
Comrade Yue!
(Begging the wind to carry it off.)

357
00:31:40,201 --> 00:31:41,999
(Begging the wind to carry it off.)

358
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Comrade Saeng!

359
00:31:43,001 --> 00:31:45,440
(I don't want to live like this.)

360
00:31:46,840 --> 00:31:47,280
Comrade Saeng!

361
00:31:47,281 --> 00:31:48,559
Comrade Saeng!
(As someone who never forgets…)

362
00:31:48,560 --> 00:31:50,400
(As someone who never forgets…)

363
00:31:51,240 --> 00:31:55,159
(I could barely breathe.)

364
00:31:55,160 --> 00:31:55,520
(If I knew I'd lose you…)

365
00:31:55,521 --> 00:31:57,319
It's me! Comrade Saeng!
(If I knew I'd lose you…)

366
00:31:57,320 --> 00:31:58,760
(If I knew I'd lose you…)

367
00:32:06,600 --> 00:32:07,760
Comrade Yue...

368
00:32:09,920 --> 00:32:10,920
Where were you?

369
00:32:11,680 --> 00:32:13,440
I've been looking for you forever.

370
00:32:33,120 --> 00:32:40,439
(Every night, pretending I can handle it.)

371
00:32:40,440 --> 00:32:44,479
(Not knowing how deep I'm sinking.)

372
00:32:44,480 --> 00:32:47,960
(I'd be fine.)

373
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:52,839
(I told myself I could live without you…)

374
00:32:52,840 --> 00:32:56,880
(A world without you seemed easy enough.)

375
00:32:57,240 --> 00:33:03,400
(But today, I realize… you've never left)

376
00:33:05,520 --> 00:33:09,879
(from this heart that
still holds onto your love.)

377
00:33:09,880 --> 00:33:13,879
(Onto the promises…)

378
00:33:13,880 --> 00:33:19,759
(that no matter how long it
takes, no one can replace...)

379
00:33:19,760 --> 00:33:21,639
If I could turn back time,

380
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:23,999
(you.)

381
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:26,800
I'd spend as much time
with you as possible. (you.)

382
00:33:29,920 --> 00:33:37,000
(I just want to forget
how happy we used to be.)

383
00:33:38,320 --> 00:33:46,320
(To wish that your smile
would slowly fade away.)

384
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:54,440
(Yet this heart keeps
waiting, never drifting off.)

385
00:33:54,720 --> 00:34:01,640
(In the end, it's me who
just won't let you go.)

386
00:34:04,120 --> 00:34:11,439
(Every night, pretending I can handle it.)

387
00:34:11,440 --> 00:34:15,639
(Not knowing how deep I'm sinking.)

388
00:34:15,640 --> 00:34:19,000
(I'd be fine.)

389
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:23,839
(I told myself I could live without you…)

390
00:34:23,840 --> 00:34:28,080
(A world without you seemed easy enough.)

391
00:34:28,280 --> 00:34:29,879
Comrade Saeng!
(But today, I realize… you've never left)

392
00:34:29,880 --> 00:34:34,720
(But today, I realize… you've never left)

393
00:34:36,520 --> 00:34:40,839
(from this heart that
still holds onto your love.)

394
00:34:40,840 --> 00:34:44,759
(Onto the promises…)

395
00:34:44,760 --> 00:34:51,080
(that no matter how long it
takes, no one can replace... )

396
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:55,800
(you.)

397
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:41,160
Excuse me, sir.

398
00:35:42,440 --> 00:35:43,440
Come in.

399
00:35:48,640 --> 00:35:49,920
I have something to report, sir.

400
00:35:52,160 --> 00:35:53,440
Someone left this for you.

401
00:36:14,640 --> 00:36:16,280
Where is the person who brought this now?

402
00:36:20,640 --> 00:36:22,760
How come you could come
out for a walk with me today?

403
00:36:23,520 --> 00:36:25,040
Aren't you usually busy?

404
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:27,080
What he did to Uncle Rapee,

405
00:36:27,760 --> 00:36:29,240
have you fogiven him yet?

406
00:36:42,120 --> 00:36:43,639
I'm happy that you've-

407
00:36:43,640 --> 00:36:45,320
finally moved on.

408
00:36:47,400 --> 00:36:49,840
That's why there's
something I want to give you.

409
00:38:06,680 --> 00:38:10,639
(As the sunlight slowly fades away, )

410
00:38:10,640 --> 00:38:14,679
(all I need is someone by my side.)

411
00:38:14,680 --> 00:38:18,919
(Let it be you, let it be you.)

412
00:38:18,920 --> 00:38:22,360
(Just sitting close, meeting
your eyes, warms my heart.)

413
00:38:22,720 --> 00:38:26,480
(Let this moment be just the two of us.)

414
00:38:26,680 --> 00:38:30,639
(Like the moon waiting
for its time to shine.)

415
00:38:30,640 --> 00:38:34,959
(Let it be you, can it be you?)

416
00:38:34,960 --> 00:38:38,480
(The one who stays by
my side and never leaves.)

417
00:38:38,800 --> 00:38:41,680
(Let it be you…)

418
00:38:56,440 --> 00:38:58,960
(Who knows what tomorrow holds, )

419
00:38:59,640 --> 00:39:03,480
(or how things might change.)

420
00:39:04,920 --> 00:39:11,680
(Just having you is all my heart desires.)

421
00:39:12,920 --> 00:39:15,399
(In the darkest of nights...)

422
00:39:15,400 --> 00:39:21,039
(Please know that whenever you look back, )

423
00:39:21,040 --> 00:39:25,159
(Through all the tomorrows, )

424
00:39:25,160 --> 00:39:27,960
(I'll still be right here,
never leaving your side.)

425
00:39:28,640 --> 00:39:29,920
Sin.

426
00:39:31,200 --> 00:39:32,640
How did you get here?

427
00:40:15,160 --> 00:40:16,600
We need to destroy the body quickly.

428
00:40:17,480 --> 00:40:19,360
Otherwise the Party
will definitely punish you.

429
00:40:21,760 --> 00:40:23,120
I'll report to the other side.

430
00:40:24,440 --> 00:40:25,680
That you were killed-

431
00:40:26,560 --> 00:40:27,840
And Comrade Fah escaped.

432
00:40:30,440 --> 00:40:31,920
Leave everything behind here.

433
00:40:34,560 --> 00:40:36,360
Remember this: Comrade Yue is dead.

434
00:40:39,800 --> 00:40:41,120
From now on, you are Sasin.

435
00:40:44,080 --> 00:40:45,680
There's someone waiting for you outside.

436
00:40:47,800 --> 00:40:49,600
Go live your life.

437
00:41:44,200 --> 00:41:46,320
Did you ever receive the letters I sent?

438
00:41:47,920 --> 00:41:49,160
Not even once.

439
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:51,160
That's such a shame.

440
00:41:53,640 --> 00:41:55,199
No need to regret it.

441
00:41:55,200 --> 00:41:57,080
There wasn't much inside anyway.

442
00:41:58,160 --> 00:41:59,160
Just...

443
00:42:00,160 --> 00:42:01,760
“I miss you” over and over again.

444
00:42:04,080 --> 00:42:05,319
Wow,

445
00:42:05,320 --> 00:42:06,800
now I want to read them even more.

446
00:42:10,360 --> 00:42:11,800
But now we're together already.

447
00:42:13,160 --> 00:42:15,440
And neither of us is going anywhere again.

448
00:42:21,360 --> 00:42:22,480
Is something wrong?

449
00:42:32,400 --> 00:42:34,320
Are you afraid other
people won't accept us?

450
00:42:40,760 --> 00:42:42,520
Your mother... right?

451
00:43:01,000 --> 00:43:02,920
I'll atone for what I've done.

452
00:43:05,560 --> 00:43:08,080
And I'll make your mother accept me.

453
00:43:11,800 --> 00:43:13,080
I'll be waiting.

454
00:43:55,440 --> 00:43:57,320
Even though murder
carries a heavy sentence,

455
00:43:57,800 --> 00:44:00,520
confessing like this may
reduce your punishment.

456
00:44:03,280 --> 00:44:04,960
I just want to pay for my sins.

457
00:44:11,000 --> 00:44:12,560
Please take care of Vin for me.

458
00:44:14,520 --> 00:44:16,320
Then don't make him wait too long.

459
00:44:19,720 --> 00:44:21,480
Thank you for helping me.

460
00:44:24,720 --> 00:44:26,000
You're welcome.

461
00:44:31,320 --> 00:44:32,640
This way, please.

462
00:44:46,000 --> 00:44:49,348
(“Scapegoat Case Reopened: Former Communist
Party Member Confesses to Police Murder”

463
00:44:49,372 --> 00:44:52,440
“Revenge for his father's false accusation
that led to his death in prison.”)

464
00:45:02,913 --> 00:45:04,953
At the time, all I knew is that

465
00:45:06,920 --> 00:45:08,799
we were waiting for
the Appeals Court to decide whether-

466
00:45:08,800 --> 00:45:11,000
your dad had arrested the wrong person.

467
00:45:13,360 --> 00:45:16,279
But I never imagined that
he had truly destroyed-

468
00:45:16,280 --> 00:45:18,200
another family this badly.

469
00:45:30,520 --> 00:45:31,600
Mom...

470
00:45:33,320 --> 00:45:34,960
the person named Sasin

471
00:45:36,840 --> 00:45:38,680
was the person I was going to see that day.

472
00:45:43,840 --> 00:45:44,840
And...

473
00:45:46,080 --> 00:45:47,600
the body in Nan...?

474
00:45:49,120 --> 00:45:51,199
It was all a misunderstanding, Mom.

475
00:45:51,200 --> 00:45:53,199
As soon as he got out of the jungle,

476
00:45:53,200 --> 00:45:54,680
he immediately turned himself in.

477
00:45:56,280 --> 00:45:58,760
He truly wanted to start a new life.

478
00:46:10,760 --> 00:46:13,080
I'm not blaming him for your dad anymore.

479
00:46:14,600 --> 00:46:16,840
Because he was partly at fault too.

480
00:46:21,760 --> 00:46:23,440
But as for everything else...

481
00:46:26,960 --> 00:46:28,360
I think...

482
00:46:30,960 --> 00:46:32,600
I still can't accept it.

483
00:46:41,720 --> 00:46:43,200
But I truly love him.

484
00:46:46,600 --> 00:46:47,560
But he is...

485
00:46:47,561 --> 00:46:49,240
I don't care what he is.

486
00:46:52,040 --> 00:46:53,600
I love him.

487
00:46:54,800 --> 00:46:56,879
When I was with him, I felt safe.

488
00:46:56,880 --> 00:46:58,360
I could be myself.

489
00:47:00,880 --> 00:47:03,040
And I was deeply happy.

490
00:47:07,240 --> 00:47:09,400
But it's against nature, dear.

491
00:47:13,680 --> 00:47:15,880
What will other people think?

492
00:47:16,600 --> 00:47:18,720
I don't care what other people think.

493
00:47:20,680 --> 00:47:22,840
All I care is what you think, mom.

494
00:47:28,640 --> 00:47:30,120
I just need you to understand me.

495
00:47:31,920 --> 00:47:33,360
That alone is enough.

496
00:49:11,520 --> 00:49:13,600
(I know you can take care of yourself.)

497
00:49:14,240 --> 00:49:15,760
(But I keep thinking all the time.)

498
00:49:16,120 --> 00:49:17,560
(About how you're doing.)

499
00:49:17,880 --> 00:49:19,880
(I don't expect you
to reply to my letters.)

500
00:49:20,040 --> 00:49:22,640
(I just hope you get to read them.)

501
00:49:23,920 --> 00:49:26,760
(I want you to know that
I'm always worried about you.)

502
00:49:44,680 --> 00:49:46,120
(Is it cold in Bangkok?)

503
00:49:46,800 --> 00:49:48,920
(It gets very cold here at night.)

504
00:49:49,360 --> 00:49:51,200
(Vin, take good care of yourself.)

505
00:49:51,480 --> 00:49:54,599
(If your allergies flare up,
hurry and take medicine.)

506
00:49:54,600 --> 00:49:55,760
(don't just leave it)

507
00:49:56,160 --> 00:49:57,280
(I miss you)

508
00:49:57,920 --> 00:49:59,520
(and worry about you so much...)

509
00:50:18,160 --> 00:50:19,640
Mom...

510
00:50:23,280 --> 00:50:24,960
Mom...

511
00:50:30,880 --> 00:50:32,040
Mom...

512
00:50:35,000 --> 00:50:36,560
I know you can't accept it.

513
00:50:40,320 --> 00:50:42,680
But you don't hate me, right?

514
00:50:43,320 --> 00:50:44,960
You don't hate me, right?

515
00:50:45,640 --> 00:50:46,640
My child...

516
00:50:58,840 --> 00:51:01,280
I will always love you, dear.

517
00:51:04,000 --> 00:51:05,920
No matter who you are,

518
00:51:08,440 --> 00:51:10,360
I'll always love you.

519
00:51:33,080 --> 00:51:34,799
(Minister, how do you feel about-)

520
00:51:34,800 --> 00:51:37,320
(the atmosphere at today's
Marriage Equality event?)

521
00:51:38,017 --> 00:51:39,109
Today is considered an important step forward.

522
00:51:39,134 --> 00:51:40,855
(“Key Points of the Marriage Equality Act” Sila
Wattanakul Deputy Minister of the Interior)

523
00:51:40,880 --> 00:51:46,479
It reflects that Thai society is
becoming more accepting of diversity.

524
00:51:46,480 --> 00:51:48,160
And it proves that-

525
00:51:48,720 --> 00:51:52,039
Thailand is moving toward
a society that is truly open

526
00:51:52,040 --> 00:51:54,000
and genuinely equal.

527
00:51:58,240 --> 00:52:00,680
I believe love has never had a gender.

528
00:52:01,720 --> 00:52:03,959
And sometimes, understanding-

529
00:52:03,960 --> 00:52:07,080
can matter even more than
what society calls "correct".

530
00:52:08,840 --> 00:52:12,160
Marriage equality is not just
about obtaining legal documents.

531
00:52:13,520 --> 00:52:19,000
It is about receiving equal rights in love.

532
00:52:39,680 --> 00:52:40,840
I'm happy.

533
00:52:44,720 --> 00:52:45,920
About what?

534
00:52:50,160 --> 00:52:52,040
Being with the person I love.

535
00:52:55,760 --> 00:52:56,760
Look at you...

536
00:52:56,761 --> 00:52:58,639
back then you barely even talked.

537
00:52:58,640 --> 00:53:00,080
But now you're confessing your love.

538
00:53:07,520 --> 00:53:10,040
Can you keep making me this happy forever?

539
00:53:10,960 --> 00:53:12,120
And How do I do that?

540
00:53:16,880 --> 00:53:18,840
We'll just grow old together.

541
00:53:45,560 --> 00:53:49,080
(As the sunlight slowly fades away, )

542
00:53:49,600 --> 00:53:53,320
(all I need is someone by my side.)

543
00:53:53,680 --> 00:53:57,600
(Let it be you, let it be you.)

544
00:53:57,840 --> 00:54:01,520
(Just sitting close, meeting
your eyes, warms my heart.)

545
00:54:01,720 --> 00:54:05,799
(Let this moment be just the two of us.)

546
00:54:05,800 --> 00:54:09,440
(Like the moon waiting
for its time to shine.)

547
00:54:09,720 --> 00:54:13,840
(Let it be you, can it be you?)

548
00:54:14,080 --> 00:54:18,400
(The one who stays by
my side and never leaves.)

549
00:54:20,120 --> 00:54:26,040
(Let it be you…)
